"""
ApexLedger GraphQL schema — root definition.

Spring GraphQL fails fast at startup if no schema resource is found, so this file
establishes the root Query type that the domain schema extends in Phase 2.

Phase 2 adds, in separate .graphqls files picked up by the
`classpath:graphql/**/` pattern:
  * custom scalars (Decimal, DateTime, UUID, CurrencyCode) with their
    RuntimeWiringConfigurer registrations,
  * Account / JournalEntry / Posting / Balance types,
  * the postTransfer mutation, carrying a client-supplied idempotency key.

Every field added later must be resolved by a controller mapping:
`spring.graphql.schema.inspection.enabled=true` reports unmapped fields at
startup rather than returning nulls at request time.
"""
type Query {
    """
    Transport-level readiness probe. Confirms the GraphQL HTTP endpoint, the
    schema and the controller wiring are all live, without touching PostgreSQL,
    Redis or Kafka. Use /actuator/health for dependency health.

    Returns the literal string "pong".
    """
    ping: String!
}
